{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"persuasive-commodious-mantid","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nADR 0116's clean pre-1.0 removal policy retired every legacy env alias. The retirement\nlanded, but its scaffolding did not: the alias table is now permanently empty and the\nmapper is an identity function nobody calls. Both are still imported, re-exported, and\niterated.\n\nMeasured on `origin/main` at `50d5a36539d`:\n\n- `src/rebar/_config_sources.py:299` — `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES: dict[str, tuple[str, str, str]] = {}`.\n  The comment above it says the table is kept empty \"so compatibility imports can observe\n  that no legacy env spellings are still mapped.\"\n- `src/rebar/_config_sources.py:302` — `_map_legacy_env(legacy, value)` whose entire body\n  is `del legacy; return value`. Its docstring calls itself a \"Compatibility shim for\n  historical imports\". Nothing in `src`, `tests`, or `scripts` calls it.\n- `src/rebar/config.py:300` — `for legacy in _LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES:` inside the cache\n  signature builder. It iterates an empty dict on every config load, so it contributes\n  nothing to the signature. Its comment still claims it covers \"Every deprecated alias\n  (EV-1/EV-3/EV-3c)\" — aliases that no longer exist.\n- `src/rebar/config.py:40` imports `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES`; `:51` re-exports\n  `_map_legacy_env as _map_legacy_env`, which is an internal shim of exactly the kind\n  ADR 0111 forbids.\n\n5 files reference the pair. The 3 test files assert on the empty table rather than on\nbehavior:\n\n- `tests/unit/test_config_alias_overlap_rename.py:99` — `assert _LEGACY_ENV not in cfg._LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES`,\n  which is trivially true against `{}` and cannot fail.\n- `tests/unit/test_config_show.py:33` — `for legacy in cfg._LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES:`, a loop\n  body that never executes.\n- `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py:24` imports the table and `:60` folds it into\n  the `accounted` set with `set(_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES)`, which contributes the empty set.\n\nEvery one of these is dead weight that reads as live machinery.\n\n## Change\n\n1. Delete `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` and `_map_legacy_env` from\n   `src/rebar/_config_sources.py`, along with the comment block describing the retired\n   alias policy.\n2. Delete the `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` import at `src/rebar/config.py:40` and the\n   `_map_legacy_env` re-export at `:51`.\n3. Delete the dead loop at `src/rebar/config.py:300` and its stale comment. The cache\n   signature keeps its canonical-env and tombstone passes, which are the two live\n   contributors.\n4. Repoint the 3 test files: drop the vacuous assertion in\n   `test_config_alias_overlap_rename.py`, drop the empty loop in `test_config_show.py`,\n   and in `test_config_surface_golden.py` remove the import and the\n   `| set(_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES)` term from the `accounted` expression.\n\nNo tombstone is needed. The aliases themselves were already retired under ADR 0116 and\ntheir user-facing warnings already live in `_deprecations.py`; this removes only the\ninert remains of the mapping machinery, which was never a user-facing surface.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py` is the discriminating test: it censuses the\n  whole env surface, so if removing the `set(_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES)` term left any env var\n  unaccounted, it fails. Confirm it passes for the right reason by checking its\n  `accounted` set is unchanged in size.\n- `tests/unit/test_config_show.py` and `tests/unit/test_config_alias_overlap_rename.py`\n  must stay green with their dead constructs removed.\n- A cache-invalidation check: set and unset a canonical `REBAR_*` override mid-process\n  and confirm the resolved config changes, proving the signature still invalidates\n  without the deleted loop.\n- `make verify` for the whole-tree effect.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC1** `grep -rn '_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES' src tests scripts` exits 1 with no output.\n- [ ] **AC2** `grep -rn '_map_legacy_env' src tests scripts` exits 1 with no output.\n- [ ] **AC3** `python -c \"import rebar.config, rebar._config_sources\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC4** `pytest tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py tests/unit/test_config_show.py tests/unit/test_config_alias_overlap_rename.py -q` exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC5** A cache-invalidation test asserts that changing a canonical `REBAR_*`\n      override mid-process yields a different resolved config, and it passes.\n- [ ] **AC6** `ruff check src tests` exits 0 with no output.\n- [ ] **AC7** `make typecheck` exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC8** `git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD` lists exactly 5 paths:\n      `src/rebar/_config_sources.py`, `src/rebar/config.py`, and the 3 named test\n      modules.\n- [ ] **AC9** `make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Ordering\n\nIndependent of the two shim-removal stories. Touches `config.py` and\n`_config_sources.py`, which neither of them touches.\n\n## Out of scope — checked, not merely unexamined\n\n- The `_deprecations.py` tombstone rows for retired env names, tracked separately. Those\n  are the live user-facing warnings and are unaffected: `config.py`'s tombstone pass over\n  `tombstones()` stays exactly as it is.\n- `_canonical_env_name` and `_CANONICAL_ENV_NAMES`, which are live and carry the 7\n  per-key override spellings.\n- The two test-corpus fixtures (`tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/table.json`,\n  `tests/fixtures/cloud_adf_corpus/bodies_00.json`) that contain `_map_legacy_env` inside\n  recorded ticket prose. They are frozen corpus data, not code references, and editing\n  them would corrupt the fixtures.","id":"25a4-1ab3-3558-4cd4","parent_id":"e12f-a994-29d3-4f72","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Delete the inert legacy env alias table and mapper"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793379577974367039,"uuid":"7a89bfb0-a528-4968-90f5-b911707156a8"}